      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactProductLogSobolev.compact_gaussian_pi_logSobolev",
      "title": "Compact finite-product Gaussian log-Sobolev inequality",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6",
          "label": "FIRST S4.E6 omitted GaussianLSI background; pinned SLT GaussianLSI/TensorizedGLSI full488lines; authored compact original-slice dimension-induction sufficient OR",
          "scope": "Actual Measure.pi centered variance-one scalar Gaussian for every n including0; true function-square/Phi-square/all-partial-square/full-sum energy L1 plus homogeneous entropy<=2 coordinate-square-sum integral. Only n,f,C2,compact support inputs. Default Pi sup norm is not Euclidean gradient energy. No RMS marginal smoothness, L1/domain/LSI certificate or positive dimension/mass premise. Finite Hilbert law/orthonormal gradient Parseval, noncompact cutoff32/33, separate T2/FIRST4.6 and all paper main/work/composition remain open. Actual3184 focused build and genuine zero/alln, positive-mass n0, signed n1 and nonseparable signed n2 consumers pass with standard3 axioms. Independent proof/fidelity/commit/shared admission remains pending."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/YuanheZ/lean-stat-learning-theory/blob/d0f506f0a695018265dccb33bcb05e2f5ca1c876/SLT/GaussianLSI/TensorizedGLSI.lean",
          "label": "Pinned external finite-coordinate GaussianLSI source",
          "scope": "External source reference only; actual authored compact original-slice proof distinct, no upstream evaluation/callable port."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.GaussianCompactProductLogSobolev"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "n is any natural number, including0. The carrier uses the default finite Pi norm/topology and Borel structure. Coordinate-square energy is literal; it is not the square of the Frechet derivative operator norm for that sup norm.",
        "Only actual f, real C2 regularity and compact support are analytic inputs. Signed f, zero f and zero square mass are included. No positivity, normalization, L1, slice, law, desired inequality or limit certificate is supplied.",
        "gamma_n is literally Measure.pi of gaussianReal0 1. Probability/finite/SFinite law properties and the actual Fin.cons product-law identification are produced by existing Mathlib primitives.",
        "The square, continuous tlogt square, all coordinate derivative squares and finite-sum energy L1 are conclusions. Every fixed original scalar/tail slice is C2compact internally; true outer conditional-entropy domains precede integral subtraction and monotonicity.",
        "Actual source scalar38 and boundedbinary39 are the two direct ASTIS mathematical parents. The dimension induction calls only a strictly smaller original tail slice, never an RMS marginal square root.",
        "The coefficient is exactly2 with no dimension loss. This is a compact finite-Pi background class, distinct from the broader external W12 theorem and from the future actual finite-Hilbert/noncompact/T2/FIRST/paper algorithm/main/work/cost composition boundary."
      ],
      "statement": "For every n>=0 and signed real C2 compactly supported f on Fin n -> Real, let gamma_n be the actual product of n independent centered variance-one scalar Gaussian laws and D_i f(x)=fderiv Real f x(Pi.single i1). The theorem internally produces L1 of f squared, f squared times log(f squared), every coordinate derivative squared and their finite sum, and proves homogeneous Ent_gamma_n(f squared)<=2 integral sum_i(D_i f)^2. Zero mass and dimension0 are included.",
      "formula": "\\gamma_n=\\bigotimes_{i\\in\\mathrm{Fin}(n)}\\mathcal N(0,1),\\quad D_i f(x)=\\mathrm{fderiv}_{\\mathbb R}f(x)[e_i],\\quad \\operatorname{Ent}_{\\gamma_n}(f^2)=\\int f^2\\log(f^2)\\,d\\gamma_n-\\left(\\int f^2\\,d\\gamma_n\\right)\\log\\left(\\int f^2\\,d\\gamma_n\\right)\\le2\\int\\sum_i(D_i f)^2\\,d\\gamma_n.",
      "boundary": "Actual Measure.pi centered variance-one scalar Gaussian for every n including0; true function-square/Phi-square/all-partial-square/full-sum energy L1 plus homogeneous entropy<=2 coordinate-square-sum integral. Only n,f,C2,compact support inputs. Default Pi sup norm is not Euclidean gradient energy. No RMS marginal smoothness, L1/domain/LSI certificate or positive dimension/mass premise. Finite Hilbert law/orthonormal gradient Parseval, noncompact cutoff32/33, separate T2/FIRST4.6 and all paper main/work/composition remain open. Actual3184 focused build and genuine zero/alln, positive-mass n0, signed n1 and nonseparable signed n2 consumers pass with standard3 axioms. Independent proof/fidelity/commit/shared admission remains pending.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce genuine compact Gaussian domains",
          "text": "C2 gives continuous actual Frechet derivatives. Compact support is preserved by each fixed directional derivative, squaring, and the continuous tlogt map with value0 at0. Continuous compact functions are integrable under the actual finite Gaussian law. Finite summation gives the full coordinate-energy domain internally.",
          "formula": "f^2,\\ \\Phi(f^2),\\ (D_i f)^2,\\ \\sum_i(D_i f)^2\\in L^1(\\gamma_n),\\qquad\\Phi(t)=t\\log t.",
          "lean": "compact_domains; HasCompactSupport.fderiv_apply/comp_left; ContDiff.continuous_fderiv; Continuous.integrable_of_hasCompactSupport; integrable_finsetSum"
        },
        {
          "title": "Handle the actual empty-coordinate probability law",
          "text": "At dimension0 the carrier is a singleton and every f is constant there. Actual probability integrals retain that constant; homogeneous entropy cancels identically and the finite coordinate sum is empty. No positive dimension or square-mass assumption is required.",
          "formula": "n=0:\\quad\\operatorname{Ent}_{\\gamma_0}(f^2)=0,\\qquad\\int\\sum_{i\\in\\mathrm{Fin}(0)}(D_i f)^2\\,d\\gamma_0=0.",
          "lean": "empty_entropy; Subsingleton.elim; actual pi probability and integral_const simplification"
        },
        {
          "title": "Split the true law and preserve original slice regularity",
          "text": "The actual Fin.cons map takes the scalar Gaussian times the n-coordinate Gaussian product to gamma_(n+1). Its continuous linear equivalence supplies the genuine measurable embedding. Fixed scalar and tail insertions are closed embeddings, so compositions with the original f preserve compact support as well as C2 regularity.",
          "formula": "(a,y)\\mapsto\\mathrm{Fin.cons}(a,y),\\qquad(\\mathrm{Fin.cons})_\\#(\\gamma_1\\otimes\\gamma_n)=\\gamma_{n+1};\\qquad f(\\cdot,y),\\ f(a,\\cdot)\\in C_c^2.",
          "lean": "split_law; original_slices; measurePreserving_piFinSuccAbove.symm; Fin.consEquivL; isClosedMap_prodMk_left/right; HasCompactSupport.comp_isClosedEmbedding"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the actual coordinate derivatives",
          "text": "The real coordinate-update chain rule differentiates the actual original slices. Updating the head gives the0th direction; updating a tail coordinate commutes with Fin.cons and gives its successor direction. These are literal directional identities, with no Hilbert gradient or operator-norm replacement.",
          "formula": "\\frac{d}{da}f(a,y)=D_0f(a,y),\\qquad D_i[f(a,\\cdot)](y)=D_{i+1}f(a,y).",
          "lean": "coordinate_derivatives; hasDerivAt_update; HasFDerivAt.comp_hasDerivAt; Fin.cons_update; Function.update_eq_self"
        },
        {
          "title": "Apply actual binary entropy to original conditional entropies",
          "text": "Compact continuity supplies a genuine global bound on F(a,y)=f(a,y)^2; joint measurability and pointwise nonnegativity are internal. The actual bounded binary producer supplies all joint/slice/marginal tlogt domains and its marginal inequality. True Fubini and integrable subtraction convert that inequality to the conditional-entropy bound below, including zero fibers/mass.",
          "formula": "\\operatorname{Ent}_{\\gamma_{n+1}}(f^2)\\le\\int\\operatorname{Ent}_{\\gamma_n}(f(a,\\cdot)^2)\\,d\\gamma_1(a)+\\int\\operatorname{Ent}_{\\gamma_1}(f(\\cdot,y)^2)\\,d\\gamma_n(y).",
          "lean": "split_square_class; split_entropy_bound; actual bounded_product_entropy_subadditivity; Integrable.integral_prod_left/right; integral_sub; integral_prod/integral_prod_symm"
        },
        {
          "title": "Use the scalar theorem and strict dimension induction",
          "text": "Apply the actual compact scalar Gaussian LSI to each original scalar slice and the induction hypothesis to each original n-dimensional tail slice. Both regularity/support inputs were constructed internally; the square root of a marginal average is never differentiated. Coordinate identities retain the exact coefficient2.",
          "formula": "\\operatorname{Ent}_{\\gamma_n}(f(a,\\cdot)^2)\\le2\\int\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(D_if(a,y))^2\\,d\\gamma_n(y),\\qquad\\operatorname{Ent}_{\\gamma_1}(f(\\cdot,y)^2)\\le2\\int(D_0f(a,y))^2\\,d\\gamma_1(a).",
          "lean": "finite_lsi strict Nat induction; actual compact_gaussian_logSobolev; original_slices; coordinate_derivatives"
        },
        {
          "title": "Integrate and assemble the full finite energy",
          "text": "The joint coordinate-square domains pull back along the actual measure-preserving map. Their outer integrals and conditional entropies are genuinely integrable, so integral monotonicity is valid. Fubini and the finite head-plus-tail sum identity combine both bounds into exactly2 times the actual total coordinate energy. The public theorem joins this inequality with the internally produced domains.",
          "formula": "2\\iint\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(D_if)^2\\,d\\gamma_n\\,d\\gamma_1+2\\iint(D_0f)^2\\,d\\gamma_1\\,d\\gamma_n=2\\int\\sum_{i=0}^{n}(D_if)^2\\,d\\gamma_{n+1}.",
          "lean": "finite_lsi; MeasurePreserving.integrable_comp_of_integrable/integral_comp; integral_mono; integral_prod/integral_prod_symm; integral_add; Fin.sum_univ_succ; compact_gaussian_pi_logSobolev"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "For every n>=0 and signed real C2 compactly supported f on Fin n -> Real, let gamma_n be the actual product of n independent centered variance-one scalar Gaussian laws and D_i f(x)=fderiv Real f x(Pi.single i1). The theorem internally produces L1 of f squared, f squared times log(f squared), every coordinate derivative squared and their finite sum, and proves homogeneous Ent_gamma_n(f squared)<=2 integral sum_i(D_i f)^2. Zero mass and dimension0 are included.",
      "lean_proof": "Produce genuine compact Gaussian domains; Handle the actual empty-coordinate probability law; Split the true law and preserve original slice regularity; Identify the actual coordinate derivatives; Apply actual binary entropy to original conditional entropies; Use the scalar theorem and strict dimension induction; Integrate and assemble the full finite energy",
      "astis_dependencies": [
